old a 7 and there are two on the board), Queens Full, or Jacks Full (unlikely given the opponent's passive play). The opponent has check-called the Flop and Turn, suggesting they have a made hand like Top Pair (Q) or Second Pair (J) that they are trying to get to showdown cheaply. Checking would waste a prime opportunity to extract more value. A moderate bet is the best play to get called by these worse hands without scaring them away.\n\nReason: You have a Full House, which is effectively the nuts in this situation given the betting history. You want to build the pot. The pot size is approximately 1000 chips (plus blinds). A bet of 500 (half-pot) is large enough to get significant value but small enough that an opponent holding a Queen or Jack is likely to call.\n\nAnswer: 500"}
