e currently in the lead with a cumulative score of +1700 and there are only 4 hands left. Being out of position post-flop (you act first on the flop, turn, and river) puts you at a disadvantage. Raising would build a larger pot that you have to play out of position, increasing the variance and the risk of a significant chip swing. Checking allows you to realize your hand's equity for free, keeping the pot small and controlling the variance to protect your lead.\n\nReason: To protect your cumulative chip lead late in the game, minimizing variance is optimal. Checking allows you to see the flop with a decent hand without inflating the pot while out of position.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
